%% Logical companion to the native SVG; generated from the same service/edge definitions.
flowchart TB
  accTitle: Inspect the local runtime
  accDescr: RabbitMQ Management inspects queue metrics, Flower observes transport task events, pgAdmin reads seven allowlisted application tables, Redis Commander inspects both Valkey shards, and the storage admin can read privileged original bytes. OpenObserve correlates safe lifecycle and delivery metadata.
  Queue["RabbitMQ quorum<br/>Persistent UUID deliveries<br/>Separate from application result status"]
  BrokerView["RabbitMQ Management<br/>:15672 · lab_monitor<br/>Queue/consumer metrics; no queue payload access"]
  Worker["Celery worker<br/>Leased, idempotent application effects<br/>Transport task events sent through RabbitMQ"]
  Flower["Flower<br/>:5555 · read-only task history<br/>Task SUCCESS differs from comparison outcome"]
  DB["PostgreSQL<br/>Job, document, result, outbox and inbox<br/>Owner revision + StreamEvent delivery ledger"]
  PG["pgAdmin<br/>:5050 · lab_viewer<br/>SELECT seven allowlisted application tables"]
  Cache["Two fixed Valkey shards<br/>Owner-channel wakes + socket lease keys<br/>Transient fan-out; durable replay lives in SQL"]
  CacheView["Redis Commander<br/>:8089 · viewer<br/>Both shards; scoped read-only Valkey ACL"]
  Original["SeaweedFS originals<br/>Stored source bytes, including quarantine<br/>Application scan/owner gates remain separate"]
  StorageView["SeaweedFS admin<br/>:23646 · privileged read-only operator<br/>Cluster-wide reads include raw originals"]
  BrokerView -.-> Queue
  Flower -.-> Worker
  PG -.-> DB
  CacheView -.-> Cache
  StorageView -.-> Original
